{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Day 36 — Feature selection & PCA\n","Objectives:\n","- PCA intuition and variance explained.\n","- Visualize components.\n","- Simple univariate selection with SelectKBest."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n","from sklearn.datasets import load_iris\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","X,y = load_iris(return_X_y=True)\n","pca = PCA(n_components=2).fit(X)\n","X2 = pca.transform(X)\n","plt.scatter(X2[:,0], X2[:,1], c=y); plt.title('PCA(2)'); plt.show()\n","pca.explained_variance_ratio_\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Exercises\n","1) Plot cumulative explained variance and choose K.\n","2) Compare PCA before vs after scaling.\n","3) Try SelectKBest on a classification dataset and compare."]}]}
